From: rmuxnet <armandas.kvietkus@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 11 May 2026 10:01:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] amdgpu: skip atom asic_init for Liverpool/Gladius on reset
 path
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="------------false"

This is a multi-part message in MIME format.
--------------false
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8; format=fixed
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit


PS4 Liverpool/Gladius have no AtomBIOS. The GPU reset path calls
amdgpu_device_asic_init() which unconditionally invokes
amdgpu_atom_asic_init() — this fails on PS4 with 'asic atom init
failed!' and leaves the system in an unrecoverable state.

cik_asic_reset() already returns 0 (no-op) for APUs, so there is
nothing to re-POST. Return early from amdgpu_device_asic_init()
for CHIP_LIVERPOOL and CHIP_GLADIUS to allow the resume path to
continue gracefully after a ring timeout.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)


--------------false
Content-Type: text/x-patch; name="0097-amdgpu-skip-atom-asic_init-for-Liverpool-Gladius-on-.patch"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="0097-amdgpu-skip-atom-asic_init-for-Liverpool-Gladius-on-.patch"

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
index 1c708eea311425d15502de18a5689426b816c9de..eceaff3c4f4f32bfb3029438774d49a11634ae21 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
@@ -883,6 +883,10 @@ static int amdgpu_device_asic_init(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 	int ret;
 
 	amdgpu_asic_pre_asic_init(adev);
+
+	if (adev->asic_type == CHIP_LIVERPOOL ||
+	    adev->asic_type == CHIP_GLADIUS)
+		return 0;
 	flags = amdgpu_device_get_vbios_flags(adev);
 	optional = !!(flags & (AMDGPU_VBIOS_OPTIONAL | AMDGPU_VBIOS_SKIP));
 

